{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792491782,"nonce":"Mg0glipXcSUANnxdTlFlMIK4IyQ=","title":"Motion groups record commands and animation indices in the static batch","message":"Scoped slice of e0a7502e3e9d71bb983572df7db0033a67da1c48262e53368ae2399bc22e583a. GpuPaintContext routes motion children into dynamic_batch but records Push/Pop in batch. bg_layer_command_count returns that static command count too, whereas apply_binding_deltas patches cached_dynamic_batch. A preceding static group can therefore make the motion opacity index point to a missing or unrelated command. The compositor dynamic dispatch also clones only primitives and discards group/path commands.\n\nTwo CPU regressions fail on 09329da2: a motion group's post-push count is 3 after an unrelated static group rather than its local index 1, and popping after the motion route closes writes commands into the wrong batch. Offscreen application regressions exercise overlapping producer children and the actual walker/cached opacity patch path including zero recovery.\n\nThis slice covers groups opened while background motion emission targets dynamic_batch: store the command owner at push, emit Pop to the same owner, snapshot that batch's command index, leave group opacity for its compositor, and dispatch the complete dynamic batch through ordered single-sample layer composition. Preserve unrepresented ancestor opacity and existing independently dispatched composite/foreground/image fallbacks. Cross-stream isolation of a group opened elsewhere remains in e0a7502; moving all commands blindly into the active batch is not the fix.","files":null}]}